========================= OOPs ============================

1. Class  - Blueprint for the Object

2. Object - Instance of Class

3. Constructor - To initialise the class variables

4. Types of Variable -
		Local
		Instance
		Static

5. Static Keyword - Directly we can access with ClassName (No need to create object)

		Static Variable - Common to each object - Class Level
		Static Method   - Inside method only Static variables are allowed

============= Pillars of OOPs ============================================

6. Inheritance -
		When one class acquire properties and methods of another class
		This is achieved by 'extends' keyword

	a) Constructor Chaining
		It is a mechanism where Object of Child class - First call constructor of Parent Class and the child class

	b) This Keyword - Reference of Current class object

	c) Super Keyword - Reference of Parent class object


7. Polymorphism

	Method Overloading       			Method Overriding

	Two Methods having Same Name			When we have Parent and Child Class

	But Different Parameters (Num or Type)		Child class can have SAME method

	In the Same Class				But different implementation

8. Encapsulation

	- Wrapping up the data and methods into one single unit called encapsulation

	- Getter and Setter methods to access the class Variable (private)

	- Access Modifier

		Public  - Everywhere
		Private - Inside Class Only
		Default - Inside package only

9. Abstraction and Interface

Abstraction  (0% to 100%)

		When we have abstract Method - declare the class as abstract class
		Abstract Method - Do not have implementation (body)
		Child class have responsibility to implement it
		We an NOT create object of abstract class

Interface = 100% abstraction
		Variable - public static and final
		Multiple inheritance
